      "knowledge_point_id": "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane",
      "problem": "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$",
